Falsifies `network_stack::ephemeral_port::verification::a_position_is_a_port_in_range_and_the_clock_never_runs_backwards`.

The defect: `port_at` takes the remainder modulo one more than the range, so the top position maps
past `HIGHEST_PORT`.

Expected to fail: the harness's range assertion on the port.

diff --git a/crates/network_stack/src/ephemeral_port.rs b/crates/network_stack/src/ephemeral_port.rs
index 4ff507d82..9a1e2923e 100644
--- a/crates/network_stack/src/ephemeral_port.rs
+++ b/crates/network_stack/src/ephemeral_port.rs
@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@ fn clock(milliseconds: u64) -> u64 {
 }
 
 fn port_at(position: u64) -> u16 {
-    LOWEST_PORT + (position % PORT_COUNT) as u16
+    LOWEST_PORT + (position % (PORT_COUNT + 1)) as u16
 }
 
 /// Machine-checked proofs, run with `cargo kani`: the clock and the position-to-port map hold
